@flags
wrapper show_report version=1 id=b0000001-0001-0001-0001-000000000001

@prompt
Hazel is a live functional environment. Every edit is a valid program, and it evaluates *around* holes (the hexagons), so there is always a value to look at.

The way to look is a **probe**: put your cursor on the `+` and press **Cmd/Ctrl+E** (or right-click, *Add probe*). The program's value appears right there, hole and all: Hazel computed everything around the missing piece.

# Task
A plant drinks 250 ml a day. A week is `250 * 7`, plus a 50 ml top-up on the new moon. Fill the hole and watch the probe; you are done when it reads **1800**.

@hint
A week is 7 days.

@reference
### Holes
Hexagons are holes. Hazel evaluates around them. Fill one by typing a value.

### Integer operations
`(+ - * /)`

### Probes
- **Add / remove a probe**: Cmd/Ctrl+E, or right-click then *Add probe*

@hints
Fill the hole appropriately.

@code
250 * ¿ + 50

@test
test answer == 1800 end
